        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set explores the methodologies, cognitive principles, and systemic structures behind effective daily planning for a Personal Knowledge Base (Personal Knowledge Base). Moving beyond simple \"to-do lists,\" these topics frame daily planning as a high-level strategic activity. They cover the integration of formal methodologies like GTD and Zettelkasten into a daily workflow, the role of cognitive science in managing attention and preventing overload, and the behavioral psychology of building sustainable habits. Furthermore, the topics investigate how the very architecture of a Personal Knowledge Base system can be designed to reduce friction and how the \"daily note\" artifact can be elevated from a mere log to a central cognitive dashboard.",
        "line_number": 28,
        "source": "topic-set_the-art-and-science-of-daily-pkb-planning_🆔20251028192710.md",
